The contents of custom_components/sleepiq/ are derived from
homeassistant/components/sleepiq/ at tag 2026.8.2. The per-file SHA-256 hashes
of that baseline are recorded in docs/UPSTREAM-BASELINE.txt, where each file
this project edits is marked `modified`.

Files added by this project, with no upstream counterpart:

  * massage.py         - massage state model and control
  * diagnostics.py     - diagnostics download
  * quality_scale.yaml - Integration Quality Scale record
  * translations/      - runtime translations (a copy of strings.json)

Modifications by this project, relative to that baseline. Three of them run
through every platform: entity names come from strings.json through a
translation key instead of a hard-coded English string, icons come from
icons.json instead of _attr_icon, and every write to the bed raises a
translated HomeAssistantError instead of letting the library's exception
escape. Every name is also imported from the module that defines it, because
mypy in strict mode does not accept either library's implicit re-exports.

  * __init__.py      - build massage objects during setup, translated setup
                       exceptions, migration of every per-side unique id from
                       the sleeper to the side, a repair issue when the
                       deprecated YAML block is imported
  * binary_sensor.py - has_entity_name and a translated name, icons.json,
                       PARALLEL_UPDATES, entities added for beds found later
  * button.py        - translated names, icons.json, PARALLEL_UPDATES,
                       translated write failures, calibration filed as a
                       configuration entity
  * config_flow.py   - masked password selector on every form, a DHCP
                       discovery step, a reconfigure flow
  * const.py         - massage entity type constants, translation keys, the
                       repair issue key; core's ENTITY_TYPES name table and
                       icon constants dropped with the hard-coded names
  * coordinator.py   - fetch massage state on each refresh, translated poll
                       exceptions, login failure raised as ConfigEntryAuthFailed,
                       the account's bed list followed as beds are added and
                       removed
  * entity.py        - has_entity_name on the base classes, the bed id as a
                       device identifier, the shared write helper, the helper
                       that adds a later bed's entities; core's sleeper_for_side
                       fallback removed, because per-side hardware is keyed on
                       the side
  * light.py         - translated name per outlet, PARALLEL_UPDATES,
                       translated write failures
  * number.py        - massage timer number entity, translated names per side
                       and end, icons.json, PARALLEL_UPDATES, translated write
                       failures
  * select.py        - massage mode and head/foot speed select entities,
                       translated names, icons.json, PARALLEL_UPDATES,
                       translated write failures, the foot warmer and core
                       climate selects keyed on the bed and the side rather
                       than on the sleeper
  * sensor.py        - translated names per sleeper, icons.json
  * switch.py        - translated name, icons.json, PARALLEL_UPDATES,
                       translated write failures
  * strings.json     - a name for every entity, massage translations, field
                       descriptions, exception messages, the repair issue;
                       core-only [%key:...] references replaced with literals,
                       which do not resolve outside core
  * icons.json       - an icon for every entity that needs one beyond its
                       device class
  * manifest.json    - custom component identity and version
